# J.A.R.V.I.S. // Environment reference
#
# IMPORTANT: the runtime does NOT auto-load a `.env` file. These are ordinary
# process environment variables: export them in your shell (or your service
# manager) before starting `python jarvis.py`. This file only documents the
# variables the code actually reads; every entry is optional and commented out.
#
# The HUD port is a CLI flag, not a variable:  python jarvis.py --port 8899
# The server binds to 127.0.0.1 unless `--remote` is passed explicitly.
# Fail-closed behaviour is not configurable from the environment.
#
# Never commit a real `.env`; it is ignored by `.gitignore`.

# --- Checkout location -------------------------------------------------------
# Override the registry root used by tooling/agentic (default: this checkout).
# JARVIS_REGISTRY_ROOT=/path/to/jarvis-skill-registry

# --- Optional arsenal outside the checkout -----------------------------------
# Directory holding data/arsenal_library.sqlite and models/random_forest_model.json.
# Read when present; the harvest tool mirrors the database there only if this
# variable is set or the directory already exists.
# Default: D:/Program Files/jarvis-arsenal on Windows, ~/.jarvis-arsenal elsewhere.
# JARVIS_ARSENAL_HOME=

# --- Optional IDE skills mirror ----------------------------------------------
# Directory that receives a copy of skills written by the autonomous ingestion
# cycle. Default: ~/.gemini/config/skills, used only if it already exists.
# Set to an empty value to disable mirroring.
# JARVIS_IDE_SKILLS_DIR=

# Root of the local Gemini/Antigravity profile read by tooling/jarvis_mcp_server.py
# (default: ~/.gemini).
# GEMINI_ROOT=

# --- Provider-backed chat (strictly opt-in) ----------------------------------
# See docs/architecture/SERVER_INFERENCE_BOUNDARY.md before enabling.
# All three are required together; provider API keys stay in the ignored
# config/api_keys.json (template: config/api_keys.example.json).
# JARVIS_CHAT_ALLOW_CLOUD=1
# JARVIS_CHAT_TOKEN=<long random bearer secret>
# JARVIS_CHAT_PROVIDERS=groq,ollama

# --- Signed integrations (required only when the integration is used) --------
# n8n webhook HMAC secret: explicit, at least 16 characters.
# JARVIS_N8N_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# Federation exchange HMAC secret: explicit, at least 32 characters.
# JARVIS_FEDERATION_EXCHANGE_SECRET=

# --- GitHub catalog tooling (tooling/sync_starred_repos.py and harvesters) ----
# First one found is used: GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN, GITHUB_TOKEN, GH_TOKEN.
# GITHUB_TOKEN=
